---
import { media } from '../data/media';
import { url } from '../data/site';
import VideoPlayer from './VideoPlayer.astro';
import ImageGallery from './ImageGallery.astro';
import DocumentLinks from './DocumentLinks.astro';
interface Props { slug: string; position: 'top' | 'detail'; }
const { slug, position } = Astro.props;
---
{position === 'top' && slug === 'pumpsync' && <section class="evidence-section"><p class="eyebrow">Product walkthrough</p><h2>See it in action</h2><p class="evidence-intro">A walkthrough of live payment cards, simulated payment events and the analytics dashboard. The visible test records demonstrate the interface and are not real digital payments; they are not measured business outcomes. This recording has no audio .</p><VideoPlayer file="media/pumpsync-walkthrough.mp4" poster={media.pumpDashboard} title="PumpSync dashboard walkthrough · 2 min 30 sec" description="The demonstration moves from live payments to a development-only payment simulator, then explores daily totals, pump summaries and payment records." /><details class="visual-summary"><summary>Read the visual walkthrough</summary><ol><li>0:00–0:30 — live payment cards show amounts, transaction identifiers and pump assignments.</li><li>0:30–0:55 — the development-only simulator generates a test payment.</li><li>0:55–1:45 — the analytics view shows totals, date controls, daily values, pump summaries and a payment table.</li><li>1:45–2:30 — the walkthrough returns to live payments and changes the branch view.</li></ol></details></section>}
{position === 'top' && slug === 'football-adaptability' && <section class="evidence-section"><p class="eyebrow">Research + demonstration</p><h2>Watch the presentation</h2><p class="evidence-intro">The full five-minute recording combines an explanation of the research with a demonstration of the player-comparison frontend. The frontend is visible from around 3:00.</p><VideoPlayer file="media/football-presentation.mp4" poster={media.footballFrontend} title="Dissertation presentation and frontend demonstration · 4 min 59 sec" description="The complete recording covers motivation, feature engineering and model selection before demonstrating player and league comparisons." /><a class="text-link" href={url('media/football-presentation.mp4') + '#t=180'}>Open the frontend demonstration at 3:00 ↗</a><details class="visual-summary"><summary>Read the presentation outline</summary><ol><li>Opening slides introduce cross-league player adaptability and the intended recruitment-analysis use.</li><li>The methodology combines per-90 statistics, team context and position-specific scoring.</li><li>Model selection compares tree-based methods and Naïve Bayes.</li><li>From approximately 3:00, the frontend selects player groups, players and leagues, then displays performance tiers and cross-league comparisons.</li></ol><p>This is a visual outline, not a transcript of the narration. The dissertation below provides the detailed written explanation.</p></details></section>}
{position === 'detail' && slug === 'pumpsync' && <section class="evidence-section"><p class="eyebrow">Interface details</p><h2>Recording, reviewing, reconciling</h2><ImageGallery images={[{src:media.pumpPayments,alt:'PumpSync live payment cards showing test amounts and pump assignments.',caption:'Live payment cards organise incoming records by amount and assigned pump. This frame uses the recording’s test data.'},{src:media.pumpDashboard,alt:'PumpSync analytics screen with total value, payment count, daily chart and payments by pump.',caption:'The analytics overview brings payment totals, daily values and pump-level summaries together.'},{src:media.pumpSignIn,alt:'PumpSync sign-in page with email and password fields.',caption:'The supplied sign-in screen is the entry point to the authenticated platform.'}]} /></section>}
{position === 'detail' && slug === 'football-adaptability' && <section class="evidence-section"><p class="eyebrow">Research evidence</p><h2>What the evaluation shows</h2><div class="results-table-wrap"><table class="results-table"><caption>Random Forest test results — dissertation, Table 7</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Position</th><th scope="col">Accuracy</th><th scope="col">F1 score</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Defenders</th><td>0.80</td><td>0.79</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Midfielders</th><td>0.77</td><td>0.75</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Forwards</th><td>0.83</td><td>0.83</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="evidence-intro">Each position uses a 30-player test set. These scores describe classification of constructed performance tiers, so they should not be read as probabilities that a transfer will succeed.</p><ImageGallery images={[{src:media.footballCrossLeague,alt:'Defender cross-league test accuracy heatmap, with train league on the vertical axis and test league on the horizontal axis.',caption:'Figure 25, dissertation page 50: defender cross-league classification accuracy. B = Bundesliga, L1 = Ligue 1, La = La Liga, P = Premier League, S = Serie A. The variation shows that model performance depends on the training and test league.'},{src:media.footballFrontend,alt:'Frontend comparison table and chart for a selected player across five leagues.',caption:'The frontend presents model outputs for a selected player across leagues. These are exploratory comparisons, not validated predictions of transfer outcomes.'}]} /><DocumentLinks file="documents/football-dissertation.pdf" title="Predicting football player adaptability" viewLabel="View dissertation" summary="The complete 70-page dissertation explains the datasets, position-specific scoring, classifier comparisons, ablation study and limitations." /></section>}
{position === 'detail' && slug === 'london-airbnb' && <section class="evidence-section"><p class="eyebrow">Model evidence</p><h2>Price drivers and prediction errors</h2><ImageGallery images={[{src:media.airbnbImportance,alt:'Random Forest feature importance chart led by bedrooms, private-room type, guest capacity, bathrooms and beds.',caption:'From my modelling section, report page 35: the tuned forest gives strong importance to property capacity and room type, with neighbourhood features also contributing. Importance measures describe this model, not causal effects on prices.'},{src:media.airbnbErrors,alt:'Base Random Forest actual-versus-predicted prices and residual scatter plots.',caption:'From report page 36: the base forest’s errors widen at higher prices. The report notes more difficulty above £300, reinforcing the need to inspect errors as well as overall averages.'}]} /><DocumentLinks file="documents/london-airbnb-report.pdf" title="Group 11 Business Analytics Report" viewLabel="View report" summary="The complete 53-page group report includes shared data preparation and each member’s modelling work. My Random Forest and Linear Regression analysis is identified as Student 2" /></section>}
